Subject: Record which cache kind each property site filled, in the AOT profile

What this does
  The AOT profiler keeps a record per property site (the `S` record: the
  receiver shapes the site's cache fills saw). This adds the kinds those fills
  installed -- an own read, a prototype read, an own write, an add-transition
  store -- as a bit set, dumped as `kinds=` on the `S` line, and `sitekinds=1`
  in the header.

Why we need it
  The generator groups sites that saw one shape and validates the group's shape
  once, then reads and writes the slot at the cache's offset. That only works
  for a site whose cache holds an own slot. A site that reads a prototype's
  method, or one that adds a property to a fresh object, has no such cell, so a
  group built from one exits or refuses on every call and the function is
  switched off. The profile recorded shapes but not kinds, so nothing could
  tell the two apart.

  A store that added the property is noted before any of the fill's early
  returns, and its post-add shape is not counted as an own-write shape: the
  profile builds only the information, the store path is not changed. The note
  needs one extra own-property lookup in the profile build only; without
  QJS_AOT_PROFILE the regvm store path is as it was.

